* dottalkpp/data/scripts/pk_gen_probe.dts
*
* THE PROBE THAT SEPARATED TWO CANDIDATE MECHANISMS, KEPT BECAUSE IT CAN STILL
* TELL THEM APART. Written 2026-09-08 as scratch under tmp/ -- which is
* gitignored, so it would have vanished and taken the only instrument that can
* distinguish these two failures with it. Promoted here, beside the three other
* .dts of this lane (pk_policy_regression, pk_durable_write, pk_durable_read),
* rather than to tools/staging: that directory holds .ps1 and .py tooling and
* not one .dts, and DOTSCRIPT resolves names out of scripts/ (see OI-034).
*
* WHAT IT ASKS. A table (EMPNO N(6,0), SID N(6,0), LNAME C(12)) with EMPNO
* declared PRIMARY came out of APPEND with SID minted and EMPNO BLANK -- IN THE
* DECLARING PROCESS. Two mechanisms explain that and they need different fixes:
*
*   A -- THE REGISTRY PATH IS DEAD. The registry generator never mints for any
*        field, and every green generation marker in this tree is really the
*        magic name "SID" doing the work.
*   B -- THE SECOND GENERATOR DESTROYS THE FIRST ONE'S WRITE. Both generators
*        call compute_next_numeric(), which restores its cursor with
*        A.gotoRec64(save); A.readCurrent(); -- and readCurrent() RELOADS THE
*        RECORD BUFFER FROM DISK. The SID scan therefore wipes the EMPNO value
*        set moments earlier, and only the last generator's field survives to
*        writeCurrent().
*
* THE DISCRIMINATOR IS THE PAIR, NOT EITHER TABLE ALONE: PKGEN1 has ONE
* generated field and it is NOT named SID, so nothing can trample it; PKGEN2
* has two. PROBE_A green with PROBE_B1 red is B. PROBE_A red is A. Both are
* defects and they are not the same defect.
*
* MEASURED 2026-09-08, before the fix: PROBE_A .T., PROBE_B1 .F., PROBE_B2 .T.
* -- mechanism B, unambiguously, and the registry path was working all along.
* Fixed at commit 86f628026 by planning every key value first and applying the
* plan in one pass after the last scan has finished.
*
* WHAT IT READS NOW, AND WHY THAT IS WORTH KEEPING: all five markers green,
* MEASURED 2026-09-08 on build Sep 08 2026 10:07:32 (65765897 dirty) -- the
* first run of this file from its promoted path, and PROBE_B1 is the marker
* that had to move: it read .F. before the fix and .T. here.
* A RED PROBE_B1 ON A LATER BUILD IS THE TRAMPLE COMING BACK, and it is the
* only marker in the tree that says so in one line. No suite runs this -- it is
* an explicit-run instrument, and it is NOT registered in kRegressionSpecs.
*
* HOW TO RUN IT: DOTSCRIPT with an ABSOLUTE path, in a session whose data lane
* is acknowledged. IT ENDS IN QUIT, deliberately, so it can be launched as a
* child process the way pk_durability_child.ps1 launches the other two -- run it
* in a session you are willing to lose. It creates, uses and ERASEs PKGEN1 and
* PKGEN2 in SANDBOX and touches nothing else.
*
* KNOWN DEBT, shared with pk_durable_write.dts and pk_durable_read.dts and
* recorded in their commit: the paths below are ABSOLUTE.
*
* EACH TABLE CARRIES A GUARD BESIDE ITS ARMS because an errored marker in this
* runtime PRINTS NOTHING rather than going red, so four green out of five is a
* lost claim wearing a clean face. COUNT THE MARKERS: there are FIVE -- THREE
* ARMS (PROBE_A, PROBE_B1, PROBE_B2) AND TWO GUARDS, one per table. PKGEN2's
* two arms share one guard, so a guard green there proves the ROW exists and
* says nothing about which of the two fields was minted; that is what the arms
* are for.

SET TALK OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

SETPATH DBF D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\DBF\SANDBOX
SETPATH INDEXES D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\INDEXES\SANDBOX
SETPATH LMDB D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\LMDB\SANDBOX

SET ALTERNATE TO D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\tmp\pkgen_probe.alt
SET ALTERNATE ON

FORMULA "PKGEN-PROBE-BEGIN"

* ---- ONE generated field, and it is NOT named SID ------------------------
ERASE TABLE PKGEN1 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 PKGEN1 (EMPNO N(6,0), LNAME C(12))
CLOSE

SELECT 1
USE PKGEN1
SET UNIQUE FIELD EMPNO PRIMARY

APPEND
? "PROBE_A_lone_declared_field_minted:" + (EMPNO = 1)

REPLACE LNAME WITH "ROW1"
? "PROBE_A_GUARD_row_exists_and_accepts_writes:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "ROW1")

CLOSE

* ---- TWO generated fields in one table -----------------------------------
ERASE TABLE PKGEN2 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 PKGEN2 (EMPNO N(6,0), SID N(6,0), LNAME C(12))
CLOSE

SELECT 2
USE PKGEN2
SET UNIQUE FIELD EMPNO PRIMARY

APPEND
? "PROBE_B1_declared_field_minted_beside_SID:" + (EMPNO = 1)
? "PROBE_B2_magic_name_SID_minted:" + (SID = 1)

REPLACE LNAME WITH "ROW1"
? "PROBE_B_GUARD_row_exists_and_accepts_writes:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "ROW1")

CLOSE

ERASE TABLE PKGEN1 CONFIRM
ERASE TABLE PKGEN2 CONFIRM

FORMULA "PKGEN-PROBE-END"

SET ALTERNATE OFF
QUIT
